  "content": {
    "id": "p20-q8-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "Using the common logarithm, determine the smallest positive integer $n$ for which $2^n$ has ten digits.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$n=30$.",
      "worked": "A positive integer has ten digits when it lies between $10^9$ and $10^{10}-1$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}10^9&\\le 2^n<10^{10}\\\\9&\\le\\log_{10}(2^n)<10\\\\9&\\le n\\log_{10}2<10\\\\\\frac{9}{\\log_{10}2}&\\le n<\\frac{10}{\\log_{10}2}\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe table gives $\\log_{10}2\\approx0.3010$, so the lower bound is approximately $29.90$ and the upper bound is approximately $33.22$. The smallest positive integer in this interval is $n=30$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 48
  },
